==Battleground==
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lowkey]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[The Face]] spawns.
**1 [[Shy Boy]] spawns.
**1 [[CyberFace]] spawns.
**1 [[I.M. Phace]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Since no enemies spawn at all until their base is hit, you can use this to your advantage and max out your [[Worker Cat]] and Wallet. When you hit the base, lure both the Shy Boy & CyberFace close to your base, and send a cheap unit such as [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] right before they reach your base. The moment that cat dies and Cyberface's [[Wave Attack]] has passed the back of your base, send in a [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critter]] - preferably one with a guaranteed [[Critical Hit|Crit]] chance and short attack animation such as [[Sunny Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Seaside Neneko]], but others can work too. After that, get the Shy Boy away from your base immediately using [[Ototo Corps|Breakerblast]] and stall him with meatshields while draining his health. After Shy Boy dies, it's just a matter of meatshielding & chip away at the remaining enemies.

Additionally, if you own a Lv.40 [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] with his [[Explosion]] [[Talents]], you can send him out first to activate the boss wave and instantly kill the Shy Boy. This makes dealing with the Cyberface a breeze.

==Trivia==
*The word いさりび ''isaribi'' in Nighttime Lure's Japanese name, いさりびヘッド ''Isaribi Head'', refers to a fire lit on a boat to lure fish at night. "Head" refers to one of the [[The Face|Face]] variants and possibly also a leader such as a minister, as the stage is found in [[Marine Ministry]].
*While it does help to lure in Nighttime Lure, the stage ironically doesn't take place at night.

